---
import DocsLayout from "@layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Heading from "@components/Heading.astro";
import Alert from "@components/Alert.astro";
import Code from "@components/Code.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Introduction">
  <Alert variant="info" title="Work in progress">
    <p>
      This page is a stub for Sprint 3 (docs shell). The full Getting Started section lands in
      Sprint 9.
    </p>
  </Alert>

  <Heading level={1}>Introduction</Heading>
  <p class="text-muted">
    Caatinga is a deployment orchestration and versioned artifacts tool for Soroban. It manages the
    full lifecycle of a contract — from source to a deployed, invokable instance — and keeps a
    record of every deployment in your own Git repository.
  </p>

  <Heading level={2}>What is Caatinga?</Heading>
  <p class="text-muted">
    Instead of tracking deployed contract IDs and WASM hashes by hand, Caatinga generates a
    versioned artifact file per project and derives browser-ready TypeScript bindings from it — no
    hosted registry required.
  </p>

  <Heading level={3}>Why not just use the Stellar CLI directly?</Heading>
  <p class="text-muted">
    You still do — Caatinga orchestrates the Stellar CLI rather than replacing it, adding dependency
    resolution across contracts, upgrade tracking, and generated bindings on top.
  </p>

  <Heading level={2}>The deployment workflow</Heading>
  <p class="text-muted">Every project follows the same six-stage flow:</p>
  <Code block>{"init → build → deploy → generate → invoke / read"}</Code>
</DocsLayout>
